objc2-core-video on PowerPC: the `objc2-metal` feature is on by default, which
builds objc2-metal and links Metal into every program that uses this crate
with default features. There is no Metal on PowerPC (it is OS X 10.11+), so
take it out of `default`. A crate that asks for the feature explicitly still
gets it (and the objc2-metal stub, see objc2-metal@*.patch).

--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -119,3 +119,2 @@ default = [
     "objc2-core-graphics",
-    "objc2-metal",
 ]
